    "body": "Run the complete isolated acceptance for DEPTH36R3 after the authorized historical support restoration.\n\nCandidate: 7bd98db21ee950aeb91c12b296b1864b5a758c3f\nSource: c58edb0c0568c3f9fe80ba014c260513a07a8e74b211b608ade4d9052f8645b3 (1267 files)\nCI: 9725334a729f9ea43b6cb62c63bf52539511f312\n\nPrevious run 34451882079: 1668 passed, 5 failed, 6 PostgreSQL skipped. One existing mobile release test still searched the superseded client.ts implementation; it now executes the shared transport and proves offline blocking, no replay and caller/generated idempotency. Four subprocess fault-injection cases were affected by the external runner recursively invoking pytest on multiprocessing spawn; the runner now guards its entry point. Runtime/business source and the 19 authorized historical support files are unchanged.\n\nFour shards collect the complete backend suite; the aggregate job requires identical collections, disjoint complete execution, passing JUnit results and unchanged source fingerprints. Packaging, independent bundle restoration and 148 synthetic loopback HTTP checks also run against the same immutable candidate. Python 3.13.5, Node 22.22.0 and the existing frozen wheelhouse are retained.\n\nAcceptance PENDING. PostgreSQL, real browser, native device and final release gates remain open. No merge, deployment, database migration or Hong Kong access is requested. Previous PR #19 and its failed logs remain preserved.",
